! mcp_bootstrap_p234.strap -- MCP printed page 234: the Input Program's
! sweep/rewind tail (V+,V T2,V CW(V T4) .. B,V TSBQ) and the tape
! status table words it indexes (V SURTX, V SURT, V RDY, V OPB, V TSAK,
! V TSA, V TSA2K), lines 1-56.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.241, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054C41  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID CA000940  DIST. OF 3/C1  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 234"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 225160, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  56 lines, all located.  Code 225160.40 .. 225204.40
! (lines 1-40), index words 225205.00 .. 225207.00 (lines 41-43), four
! SYNs printing their values in the LOCATION column (lines 44-47), then
! data 225210.00 .. 225214.00 and a last instruction at 225215.00
! (line 56, a half word; next location 225215.40).  Line 1 at
! 225160.40 joins p.233's last row (225160.00, a half word).  Line 53
! is line 52's second DD field (225213.01), no card of its own.
! Asterisks after the LOCATION on lines 17 and 40.  Remarks are
! sequence numbers -0916 .. -0962; lines 4, 5, 18-21, 40, 41, 43,
! 48-51, 53 print none (the run skips 0948-0949, 0951, 0956-0958 there).
! Line 6 prints "-EXIT FROM SIMPLE TRANSITION", line 52 "-REWIND,
! SEQUENCE CRIT-0959".  Lines 42, 44-47, 54-56 print a lone "-" in the
! remark field before the sequence number.
!
! LABEL / GLYPH SPELLINGS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * line 29 "BXVCZ" = BXVGZ: worn crossbar.  Prints 225175.31 C2 =
!     V SWP2 (225175.00) + .31, which is BXVGZ's offset (p.233 line 51
!     BXVGZ,$.64 .71 = .40 + .31); BXVLZ on lines 24/30/34 adds .30.
!   * line 46 "V CPB" = VOPB: open O.  Landed pp.229/230/232 spell VOPB
!     (C22-6728 TS table "VOPB Flag Bit .25"); the same row prints
!     000000.31 = .25.
!   * line 6 "V CP" = VOP (landed decks); VOP+VTSB prints 225224.00.
!   * lines 50/51/55 "TSA2", "TSA2K": the glyph after A has the curved
!     top of the 2 in "V T2"/"V NLB2", not the flat top of the Z in
!     "BXVLZ" (900 dpi).  Written VTSA2, VTSA2K (no other deck spells
!     either).
!   * line 10 name "V NLB2" (sheet read ALB2): line 16 B,V NLB2 prints
!     225165.50 = this row's 225165.40 + B's .10.
!   * line 49 "VF,-V CBR" = VCBR, landed p.233 at 225122.00; prints
!     225122.00-.
!   * octal fields "CCCCCC.CC", "CCC" are 0s (round glyph in an octal
!     field).  Hex bytes settled by assembly: "C0" is 00 on lines 16 and 40
!     (B), but a real C0 on line 11 (BZXVGZ; same open ink);
!     "C1"/"C5"/"CD" are 01/05/0D; "C2" (BXVLZ/BXVGZ) and "C9" (CB-) are
!     real.  Line 1's byte is B8 (straight left stem at 900 dpi; the
!     finding-aid sheet read 88).
!   * line 52 "CD(BU,1),C,1" is DD(BU,1),0,1: worn D stem, prints 0 / 1.
!
! THE SYN ROWS.  Line 44 prints "225201.00+  -00000000  BU,30 ,10",
! line 45 "000000.32+ +00000000 BU,01 ,10", 46 "000000.31+ ... BU,01
! ,10", 47 "000000.00+ +00000004 NULL" -- V TSAK is an integer 4, as
! V H SYN,32 is on p.213.  They get !SYM, not !CHECK.
!
! CARD SERIALS.  Right-hand serials run 0A000940 .. 0A000990 (header
! CA000940).  Pairs share a serial: lines 4/5 (943), 18/19 (956), 26/27
! (963), 48/49 (984), 52/53 (987).  No serial is skipped.

